fix(ca_assembler): three root causes — on_session_end per-turn destroy, context_length default, missing _turn_index

Root causes:
1. on_session_end fires every turn (not only at session end). Had
   engine destroy logic that was dead code before register(), became
   active after register fix — killed engine after turn 1.
2. Hermes pre_llm_call hook doesn't pass context_length. CA always
   used Config.CONTEXT_LENGTH (32K) regardless of model (91.5K for
   deepseek-v4-flash). Added model→context window lookup table.
3. _rebuild_messages_from_cache didn't inject turn_index into
   reconstructed messages → idx_to_turn fell back to list position →
   head/middle/tail layering broke after switch to per-turn L2 storage.

Changes:
- __init__.py: _on_session_end → no-op; _context_length from model
  lookup in on_session_start; 15 INFO-level diagnostic logs
- ca/__init__.py: per-turn L2 storage (not cumulative snapshot);
  _rebuild_messages_from_cache simplified + injects _turn_index;
  crash fallback now writes l2_text; 7 INFO logs
- ca/config.py: _MODEL_CONTEXT_WINDOW table + context_length_for_model()

Removed: fingerprint dedup in _rebuild_messages_from_cache (TODO add
back at appropriate layer — prevents duplicate pollution from network
retry storms).

Tests: 107 passed, 2 skipped.
